From: Priyadharshini Gowthaman <pgowtham@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM:PROTOCOL:sigma_dut: Add SecProfile_AltBehavior and
 PreviousTK CAPI, WAR SP_List/SMD hostapd config (win_qsdk.common only)

Add two new CAPI parameters used by testbed STA negative test cases
(e.g. SP-5.10.3, SP-5.10.4):

- SecProfile_AltBehavior (String, "0" or "1") in cmd_ap_set_security(),
  stored in a new dut->ap_security_profile_alt_behavior field
  (sigma_dut.h), defaulted to -1 in cmd_ap_reset_default(). The
  security_profiles config-writer block now emits
  "security_profile_alt_behavior=%d\n" using this field.
- PreviousTK in cmd_ap_get_parameter(), following the same structure
  as the existing UHR/WPA3 "TK" branch: runs
  "hostapd_cli -i <ifname> previous_tk <STA_MAC_Address> -0", reads
  the result from a temp file, and returns it as "TK,<value>".

WAR: the SP_List/SP_PMKSACachingPrivacy security_profiles
config-writer block (ap.c, cmd_ap_config_commit()) also unconditionally
emits a block of hardcoded hostapd config values whenever
dut->ap_security_profiles is set, in place of properly deriving them
from the SP_List/SecProfile_AltBehavior/SMD CAPI inputs:
  wpa_passphrase=12345678
  pasn_groups=19
  rsnxe_capab_mask=2000000000
  wds_sta=1
  fils_discovery_max_interval=20
  smd_ap=1
  smd_partner=00:00:BA:5E:BA:11
  smd_identifier=11:22:33:44:55:66
  uhr_dl_drain_duration_tu=500
  smd_timeout=250
  smd_max_peer_apmlds=7
This is tracked as a workaround pending proper CAPI-driven derivation
of these values; only the two duplicate-write/dead-code artifacts
below are cleaned up here, the hardcoded values themselves are left
as-is intentionally.

Also fixes two copy-paste artifacts introduced while iterating on the
security_profiles block: the "if (dut->ap_security_profiles) {...}"
block was being written twice in a row (writing "security_profiles="
twice), and the original ap_rsnxe_capab_mask handling had been left
commented out twice with no replacement, silently breaking
SP_PMKSACachingPrivacy. Restore a single security_profiles block and
a single, active ap_rsnxe_capab_mask block.

Adds patches:
  186-UPSTREAM-PROTOCOL-sigma_dut-Add-SecProfile_AltBehavior-PreviousTK-CAPI-WAR.patch

Patch-dependency: 174-UPSTREAM-PROTOCOL-sigma_dut-Write-pasn_groups-for-SP_List-AKMs.patch
Change-Id: I9e79f1eac7fb9aa0cd917dc8a3f268b71805c69b
Signed-off-by: Priyadharshini Gowthaman <pgowtham@qti.qualcomm.com>
